historical_patches.text:
Server maintenance has started! After their completion, the following changes will be expected in the game:
◉ Added the second "Anomalous Winter" Combat Set;
◉ Now the players in the leaderboard with the same score occupy the same position;
◉ Fixed the display of the combat kit after purchase;
Minor corrections;
◉ Minor fixes.
Regards
EXBO Team.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/cfb077ded6bc4357735b1a9e79b2fcc33606364d.png
Ghouls
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/36ee1454ceaff1d6c154a357ae7f872b2e85c848.png
• Added minimum 5 seconds time interval between the ghouls' grabs;
• Added an opportunity to rotate the camera while the ghoul is grabbing you;
• Decreased the grab time to 2 seconds;
• Reduced the ghouls' movement speed by 10%. 
Settings
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/ddb8f654244f5e1b3a7d3f49579859e46120f8f1.png
• Added a setting for hiding the aiming point/cross on the screen;
• Added “Hitmaker display time” setting;
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/765e04b1ecda209c71e158fc3827b6dd1d960846.png
• Added “Adjust aiming sensitivity” setting;
Other changes
• Adjustments the displayed status of transferability of items when buying packs in the store;
• Fixed the issue with voice chat being turned off when switching between locations; 
• Fixed the players ragdoll's position and rotation after the death;
• Fixed a bug with Master of the Zone stun with a flashbang grenade, now he is not stunned after the immunity subside.
• Fixed an issue with collision of some slopes;
• Fixed server desynchronization of the position of grenades and bolts when throwing them; 
• Fixed an issue with the player being unable to pick up an artifact from the interactable object;
• Fixed an issue with the player being unable to pick up an artifact at certain angles on the slopes;
• Reconfigured artifacts spawn in some locations after the eruption; 
• Fixed an issue with displaying an ability to set the tent when it is impossible;
• Fixed an issue with the whirlpool instantly killing the player when leaving it;
• Removed the function of pushing back a character when taking damage from another player in melee combat;
• Fixed recoil compensation not working on consecutive clicks via firing sniper rifles.
Thank you for your attention,
and good luck hunting in the Zone!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/c196554720744ed5fab6050300bb15c3879951bf.png
Server maintenance has just started! When it is completed, you are to expect this one little but still important change:
Until the end of this season, you can trade armour and weapon components of all the ranks to the advanced spare parts at the Exchanger. The following number of components can be traded for one spare part:
• Pack of Weapon/Armour Components (Master) — 8;
• Pack of Weapon/Armour Components (Veteran) — 14;
• Pack of Weapon/Armour Components (Stalker) — 20;
• Pack of Weapon/Armour Components (Newbie) — 25.
Thank you for your attention,
And good luck on the Boral Island, Researchers!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/e73c04d6290c68bed91d40a9eff0ec1f768074a6.jpg
Session battles adjustments
• The DeathMatch mode is now available. DeathMatch switches with Arms Race every hour;
The frequency of mode switches was implemented in order to collect data on the popularity of each mode. The time intervals will be adjusted in the future;
• Personal storage can now be opened before the respawn only. This prevents receiving grenades from personal storage;
• Fixed the GOST-17 respawn spots: players no longer spawn at the same point;
• Respawn in session battles can be activated by pressing “Space”;
• Fixed the bug that made players disappear in the final score window after leaving the match;
• Players from one squad are now prioritized to be in one match;
• Grenades from the session battles now disappear after death;
• Changed the level required to purchase Anomalous Serum from level 75 to 15 at Spartak stock;
• Increased rewards on Wormhole, Streets of Pripyat, Collapse and Colosseum by one and a half times;
• Locked Flamethrower, Tinderbox, Frostthrower, and Coldcutter in session battles until they are reworked;
• Fixed disappearing consumable items in session battles with custom gear;
• Fixed the game client freezing on session battles respawn.
Balance changes
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/0d6d68f260e90a997b7418a2505970b73982772d.png
Other changes and fixes
• Fixed an issue that occurred when firing in bursts.
• The Convert’s Bite skin now can be used for the Antiterror melee weapon.
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/26a0c396ca427f89b3899e219ca2d0b2d8637e95.png

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/3d19bcb3ea1e33f8d3b34d189c7a269c9c1cc9ba.jpg
Without stopping the game servers, the following changes have been implemented:
• Fixed incorrect counting of protoanomalies in daily and weekly quests;
• 750 Trade coins;
• Hex in the final Morph and Mess quest now appears correctly;
• Added unique Hideout decor as a reward for completing the Morph and Mess quest line.
Everyone who completed the quest and didn't get the decor — you'll get it soon!
⚙️ Due to this inconvenience, we have prepared a promo code as a compensation:
SCX14MAY2025-SORRY
UPD: The promo code is valid until May 16 inclusively
By activating the promo code, you will receive:
• 10 Anomalous Champagnes;
• 15 Forgotten Supplies crates;
• 10 Advanced tools;
• 20 Advanced spare parts;
• 3 Breach Injections.
Sincerely,
EXBO Team

The following changes have been made without stopping the game servers:
• Increased rewards for completing optional objectives;
• Increased rewards on higher difficulty levels;
• Increased the number of optional objectives required to boost rewards;
• Reduced currency rewards for main objectives.
Sincerely,
EXBO Team

The following changes have been made without stopping the game servers:
• Restored the offer with the neurodegenerant at Drossel — now requires 9 pcs;
• Replaced the offer for 250 Scarlet Minerals with 250 Purple Minerals;
• The offer for 100 Scarlet Minerals remains unchanged;
• The Advanced Electrode offer — now requires 9 pcs instead of 3;
• The Golden Minerals offer — now requires 12 pcs instead of 6.
Sincerely,
EXBO Team

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41581512/8bb4e81fd28087916d62c2b4b78e7ebc61a42240.pngThe following changes have been made without stopping the game servers:
• Adjusted the number of Gates Keycards dropping in airdrops on Forge-11;
• Fixed an issue where airdrops did not disappear after being fully looted;
• Updated event spawn logic at outposts — airdrops will now preferentially land near the center of the Forge-11;
• Revised airdrop loot composition;
• Balanced reward distribution to ensure fairer payouts.
The changes apply to new instances of the Forge-11 location.
Sincerely,
EXBO Team

The following changes have been made to the game without stopping the game servers:
• Adjusted the difficulty of NPCs and mutants;
• Increased the sell value of filler items;
• Increased the drop chance of Inverter schematics;
• Reduced the centrifuge operation time by 10 seconds.
To ensure the centrifuge timer displays correctly, please update the game.
• Increased the amount of Onyx obtained from clearing mutants and from safes;
• Increased the drop chance of Phantom Keys;
• Reduced distortion damage — it now starts applying later;
• Increased the amount of Memoria in areas on high-population servers;
• Disabled some NPC patrols in Inside Out areas.
The changes will take effect after updating and restarting the game.
Respectfully,
EXBO Team

Server maintenance is completed, game servers are back online. The following changes are now available in the game:
• The Coliseum ranked season has officially concluded. Congratulations to everyone who managed to climb to the higher leagues and secure their place among the strongest fighters! 
As for the rewards, they will be distributed on September 2 — we need time to carefully verify the results and ensure the integrity of the final standings;
• Player search and mail systems are working correctly again and are no longer case-sensitive for nicknames;
• Fixed an issue with the Taxidermist achievement. If you had already met all the requirements before the update, simply eliminate one more mutant of any kind, and the achievement will be automatically awarded.
Jump in, test the changes — and have a nice raid!
